{"title":"Career Roadmap — Quality Engineer","role":"Quality Engineer","summary":"A Quality Engineer ensures that materials, components, manufacturing processes and finished products meet defined quality, reliability, safety and performance requirements. In Metallurgical & Materials Engineering, the role is especially relevant to steel, automotive, aerospace, manufacturing, welding, foundry, casting, forging and advanced materials.","facts":{},"about":[{"label":"Direct alignment","text":"Very High — Metallurgical & Materials Engineering provides strong knowledge of material properties, microstructure, processing, testing and failure mechanisms, which are central to quality engineering."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Metallurgy, materials testing, manufacturing processes, quality tools and inspection"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Quality Engineer → Senior Quality Engineer / Supplier Quality Engineer"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Quality Manager, Quality Systems Engineer, Reliability/Quality Specialist"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Quality Head, Plant Quality Manager, Supplier Quality Director or Quality Systems Director"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Core learning","Practical outcome"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Mathematics, chemistry, physics, engineering fundamentals"},{"text":"Understand engineering materials"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Metallurgy, materials science, manufacturing and testing"},{"text":"Perform material-quality evaluation"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Quality control, statistics, NDT, failure analysis, process capability"},{"text":"Analyse manufacturing defects"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Quality systems, audits, reliability, supplier quality, process improvement"},{"text":"Execute a complete qua